## TODO: source-remote-ids-as-strings

What is left of the multi-source domain model. Phases 1 (nexus-prototype-merge) and 2
(source-identity-refactor) are done; phase 3 landed over 2026-07-20 as nine commits and
is described below only where it did NOT finish.

### Done, do not redo

The neutral domain types, the Rust-owned translation, and the single Browse page all
shipped. Rust now parses ModWorkshop listings, files, links and mod details into typed
structs (commands/domain.rs, wire structs deserialize leniently, public types are
required-field), Nexus search maps onto the same ModSummary, ModSummary is no longer
assignable to Mod so a list entry cannot be used as a full one, update status is an
explicit enum rather than magic version strings, and one Browse page carries a source
switcher (SourceSelect) with per-source mod counts.

### Dropped: source-qualified cache keys

This was going to key the renderer caches by source once both shared them. It is
OBSOLETE, not deferred: the owner chose a two-subwindow Browse page, so each source keeps
its own content component and local state. Verified 2026-07-20 that NexusBrowsePage
touches none of modCache, browseCache, thumbnailCache or installedMetaCache, so there is
no collision to key against. The one cache that does hold both sources (SourceSelect's
count cache) is already keyed by game AND source. Only revisit if the two pages are ever
merged into a single data path.

### What actually remains

Remote ids become strings across the renderer, and install_nexus_download stops writing
the legacy `id = -(nexus_mod_id)` / `file_id = nexus_file_id` values.

Blocked, and NOT merely by time:
- The reason for strings is Steam Workshop's PublishedFileId overflowing the JS safe
  integer range. Steam is not a source, so today this solves nothing.
- The negative id is load-bearing right now: it is what makes useModData skip a Nexus mod
  instead of looking it up on ModWorkshop, and what computeHealthSummary keys
  "unidentified" off (4 call sites as of 2026-07-20). Removing it needs a replacement
  signal first.
- Those ids are already written into users' .modrex.json files, so changing the scheme
  needs a state migration or real installs lose their identity.

Do this when a source with oversized ids actually lands, not before.

